  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRC is no PG-13 game, everyone understands that who has played the game for more than 10 minutes. There is a lot of lewd people, avatars, and etc. Now this is an issue and users can get banned for it if it becomes public and someone gets caught, but they do not care if you do it privately. I think there could be a way better alternative to this however especially with the new edition of avatar icons and people putting lewd pics in that. Instead of just a button to confirm that you are over the age of 13, why not either add another button to confirm if you are over the age of 18 or have a place to put your age in. This way for anyone under 18, all lewd marked avatars and/or pics (if they add an option to mark it) can be hidden with a crossout, and anyone over can view with the option to disable it if they so please. Also adding an option in the safety menu to just turn off NSFW avatars animations (as they mostly are toggles) could be an option as well so it doesnt hide it in its original form which is most of the time SFW. This would fix a number of issues and stop people from getting banned for uneeded reasons, wanting to be themselves and wanting to be lewd, and prevent any legal issues for VRC.\n\nYes, people can lie about their age just as they could on pornhub, thats why the tos and click to confirm you are over the age is there, if the person lies it is then them at fault and they can get banned, it would not be VRC's. That does not inhibit this feature request at all",
